-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 29 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - rodrigo@lyraos.com.br

- Update to 0.2.1:
  * Disable the WebKit DMA-BUF renderer at startup, so WebKitWebProcess no
    longer aborts with heap corruption on exit (lyra-downloads#5,
    vega#166). The backend and apps opened for files and folders do not
    inherit the variable.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 25 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - rodrigo@lyraos.com.br

- Update to 0.2.0:
  * Replace the GTK4/libadwaita interface with a Tauri 2 (WebKitGTK)
    interface in the style of Vega: sidebar with filters, live rows with
    progress, speed, time left and connections, reorderable queue, new
    download sheet with server probe, details, preferences and search.
  * Keep the lyra-downloads binary, the org.lyraos.Downloads app id and
    the --add-url contract used by the Firefox native host.
  * Build with gtk3, webkit2gtk 4.1, javascriptcore and libsoup 3 instead
    of gtk4 and libadwaita.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Sep 21 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - rodrigo@lyraos.com.br

- Update to 0.1.3:
  * Ship English, Brazilian Portuguese and Spanish catalogs with English fallback.
  * Translate download errors, notifications and application metadata.
  * Verify complete catalogs, placeholders and real gettext runtime selection.
  * Confirm backend readiness with a read-only health reply before sending
    an operation; never replay a mutating request after transport failure.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Sep 19 18:20:00 UTC 2026 - rodrigo@lyraos.com.br

- Update to 0.1.2:
  * Reserve the Firefox-owned filename during automatic handoff even
    when pause removed the placeholder, so browser cancellation cannot
    unlink the file being written by aria2 in the same download folder.
  * Keep manual downloads unchanged and preserve existing numbered files.
  * Add a real-aria2 regression for browser cleanup and idempotent handoff.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Sep 19 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - rodrigo@lyraos.com.br

- Update to 0.1.1:
  * Persist browser handoff revocations, including requests arriving late.
  * Confirm aria2 cancellation before acknowledging Firefox fallback.
  * Preserve completed downloads during handoff recovery.
  * Migrate SQLite schema to v2 without dropping tasks or preferences.

